# GDScript Conventions

## File & Folder Layout

- One feature per directory: always a paired `.tscn` + `.gd`.
- Reusable UI pieces live in `components/`; full screens in `menus/`.
- Autoloads (singletons) live in `autoloads/`.

## Node Access

Use `%UniqueNodeName` (percent-sign) to access nodes from scripts — never `$Path/To/Node` chains.

```gdscript
# ✅
%SearchBtn.pressed.connect(...)
%ContentArea.add_child(view)

# ❌
$VBox/HBox/SearchBtn.pressed.connect(...)
```

## API Callback Pattern

All `ApiClient` methods use a single trailing `Callable` with the signature:

```gdscript
func(success: bool, data: Variant) -> void
```

- `success == true`: `data` is a parsed `Dictionary` or `Array`.
- `success == false`: `data` is a human-readable error `String`.

```gdscript
ApiClient.get_note(note_id, func(ok: bool, data) -> void:
    if not ok:
        show_error(data)
        return
    display_note(data)
)
```

## Scene Instantiation

Preload scenes as constants at the top of the script:

```gdscript
const NoteViewScene := preload("res://menus/note_view/note_view.tscn")
# ...
var view := NoteViewScene.instantiate()
%ContentArea.add_child(view)
```

## Inter-Scene Communication

Scenes communicate via **signals**, not direct references. The parent (`main_menu`) wires child signals after instantiation:

```gdscript
func _wire_view(view: Node) -> void:
    if view.has_signal("note_requested"):
        view.note_requested.connect(_open_note)
```

## Thread Safety

`AccountManager.unlock_account()` and `update_current_account()` are safe to call from a background thread.  
They must **not** emit signals directly — call `notify_unlocked()` from the main thread afterward.

## `AccountManager` return-value convention

Mutating methods return `""` on success and a human-readable error string on failure:

```gdscript
var err := AccountManager.add_account(...)
if not err.is_empty():
    show_error(err)
```
